    <statement><p>The rate (in liters per minute) at which water drains from a tank is recorded at half-minute intervals. Use the average of the left- and right-endpoint approximations to estimate the total amount of water drained during the first 3 min.</p>
<tabular bottom="minor" left="minor" top="major" valign="top">
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<col halign="center" right="minor"/>
<row bottom="minor">
<cell><m>t</m>  min</cell>
<cell>0</cell>
<cell>0.5</cell>
<cell>1</cell>
<cell>1.5</cell>
<cell>2</cell>
<cell>2.5</cell>
<cell>3</cell>
</row>
<row bottom="major">
<cell>rate in l/min</cell>
<cell>56</cell>
<cell>54</cell>
<cell>52</cell>
<cell>50</cell>
<cell>48</cell>
<cell>46</cell>
<cell>44</cell>
</row>
</tabular>
<p>Answer: <fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/> liters.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>150</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Let <m>\Delta x = 0.5</m>. Then</p>
<p><m>R_N = 0.5 (54+52+50+48+46+44) = 147 \:</m> liters</p>
<p><m>L_N = 0.5 (56+54+52+50+48+46) = 153 \:</m> liters</p>
<p>The average of <m>R_N</m> and <m>L_N</m> is <m>\frac {1}{2}(147 + 153) = 150</m> liters.</p>
</solution>
